issue(id="0017" status="open")
  title Publish an npm-ready wasm build for the HTML to Pug converter
  user-story
    as-a JavaScript or web-tooling user
    i-want to run the puggers HTML to Pug converter from npm through a wasm-backed package
    so-that editors, browser tools, and Node workflows can use the converter without shelling out to the Rust CLI
  premise.
    The Rust HTML importer is becoming useful beyond the CLI, and future npm
    users should be able to call the same conversion behavior from JavaScript
    without a native install step. This task should define and implement the
    first npm-facing wasm build for the HTML to Pug converter, reusing the
    existing converter core instead of introducing a parallel implementation.
    The package surface should be small at first, but stable enough that
    editor integrations, browser demos, and Node-based tooling can depend on
    it. Any wasm-specific limitations, such as DOM parser availability,
    bundler assumptions, binary size, or synchronous versus asynchronous
    initialization, should be documented where users will find them.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Add an npm-consumable wasm package or package entry point that exposes the HTML to Pug converter from JavaScript.
    criterion Support at least one Node-oriented usage path and document whether browser bundlers are supported, experimental, or out of scope for the first release.
    criterion Reuse the existing Rust converter behavior and options rather than maintaining a separate JavaScript conversion implementation.
    criterion Add focused tests or examples that call the JavaScript API and assert converted Pug output for representative HTML input.
    criterion Add a repeatable build command for producing the wasm/npm artifact, and make sure it can be run from a clean checkout with documented prerequisites.
    criterion Document the initial JavaScript API, initialization model, option mapping, and known wasm limitations.
    criterion Add a Knope change file using `default` frontmatter that summarizes the new npm/wasm converter surface.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Decide whether the first package should be a dedicated npm package, an export from an existing package, or a generated artifact staged for later publishing.
    item(status="open") Confirm the wasm target can use the same HTML parsing path as the native converter, or document any necessary parser substitution before exposing the API.
    item(status="open") Decide how much browser support is required for the first task versus leaving browser bundler coverage to a follow-up.
